        "authorUrl": "",
        "commentDate": "2020-05-12T17:22:19",
        "htmlComment": "<p>ترجمه‌ای که ادوارد فیتزجرالد کرده برای این شعر به نظر من اصن منظور شعر رو نمیرسونع خصوصا مصرع اول<br />IX.<br />Each Morn a thousand Roses brings, you say;<br />Yes, but where leaves the Rose of Yesterday?<br />And this first Summer month that brings the Rose<br />Shall take Jamshyd and Kaikobad away.<br />This quatrain owes its origin to three separate ruba'iyat, viz.: O. 135 (ll. 3 and 4) C. 500 (ll. 1 and 2), C. 481 (ll. 3 and 4).</p>",
